      "title": "Legacy Proration Refund Discrepancies in Wallet Service",
      "content_summary": "Addresses incorrect refund amounts and duplicate charges resulting from proration errors in the legacy Wallet Service billing flow.",
      "content_body": "When a subscription is upgraded mid-cycle, users may report that refunds are not reflected or that they were charged twice for the same period. This issue typically stems from data quality inconsistencies in the legacy ledger or failures in the third-party payment gateway's webhook delivery. Before the introduction of the new commerce engine, agents were required to run a manual data repair script to force-sync the proration records. If the script failed, manual reconciliation of the transaction logs was necessary, often involving escalation to the payment vendor to confirm the original charge status."
